\section{Flows and Their Applications} 
Flows have emerged as a powerful tool, encompassing a broad range of models and models-to-data relationships. Nonetheless, certain fundamental aspects are often overlooked in existing publications. 
\subsection{Flows and Data Relations} 
A flow can be regarded as a bi-directional connection between data sets, enabling seamless interchanging of observations and interpretations. 
\subsection{Flow Transformations} 
Given a flow, certain transformations can be applied without compromising their standardization. 
\subsection{Flow Consistency} 
A flow's consistency can be seen as a straightforward concept: when a flow's observations and interpretations coincide, the flow is consistent. 
\subsection{Flow Learning} 
A flow's learning process can be viewed as the development of a new interpretation, anchored to existing observations. 
\subsection{Flow Inference} 
A flow's inference can be regarded as the refinement of a new observation, supported by existing interpretations. 
\subsection{Introduction to Standardizing Flows} 
We draw upon the insights from Lattice Field Physics, capitalizing on the unique aspects of standardizing flows while remaining adaptable for a variety of domain-specific applications. 

